# When to bypass RTK compaction

The Shell hook rewrites `git diff` to `rtk git diff`. Keep that compact output.

If a specific line, path, or hunk is missing, retry **once**. Do not disable RTK for ordinary status or diff.

```
# ❌ BAD — RTK_DISABLED=1 on every git status
# ✅ GOOD — compact first; if a hunk is missing:
RTK_DISABLED=1 git diff
# or: rtk git diff --no-compact
# or: Read / Grep a known file (those tools skip the Shell hook)
```

`RTK_DISABLED=1 <cmd>` makes `rtk rewrite` pass through (our hook then runs the original). Failures may print a tee path under `~/.local/share/rtk/tee/` — read that before re-running. Do not loop.
